From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:22:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 369/488] V2 runner sampling: one temperature test a block, the
 Philox draws unconditional

The Gumbel sampler and the sink candidates tested each element's bound and the
token's temperature before drawing its Philox word, so every draw sat in its own
conditional block and nvcc recomputed the key schedule (the same for every
element of a token) for each: 72 more integer adds than Triton's kernel. As in
Triton, the temperature is tested once around the block's elements and each
draw comes before the element's bound check; the scores are unchanged.
